====Preposition====
[[File:Encima.png|thumb|A {{w|GIMP|green pepper}} '''on''' (with its position being the upper surface of) a box.]]
{{en-head|prep}}

# {{n-g|Indicating position or location.}}
## Positioned at the [[upper]] surface of, [[touch]]ing from [[above]].
##: {{ux|en|A vase of flowers stood '''on''' the table.}}
##: {{ux|en|Please lie down '''on''' the couch.}}
##: {{ux|en|The parrot was sitting '''on''' Jim's shoulder.}}
##: {{ux|en|We should go sailing '''on''' the lake together sometime.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1845|author=w:Henry Wadsworth Longfellow|title=The Bridge
|passage=I stood '''on''' the bridge at midnight.}}
## Positioned at or resting against the outer surface of; attached to.
##: {{ux|en|He had a scar '''on''' the side of his face.}}
##: {{ux|en|There is a dirty smudge '''on''' this window.}}
##: {{ux|en|The painting hangs '''on''' the wall.}}
##: {{ux|en|The fruit ripened '''on''' the trees.}}
##: {{ux|en|Should there be an accent '''on''' the "e"?}}
## [[covering|Covering]].
##: {{ux|en|He wore old shoes '''on''' his feet.}}
## [[at#Preposition|At]] or in (a geographical location or position).
##: ''The lighthouse that you can see is '''on''' the mainland.''
##: ''The suspect is thought to still be '''on''' the campus.''
## [[at#Preposition|At]] (a relative spatial position).
##: ''We live '''on''' the edge of the city.''
##: '''''on''' the left, '''on''' the right, '''on''' the side, '''on''' the bottom''
## Near; [[adjacent]] to; [[alongside#Preposition|alongside]]; just off.
##: {{ux|en|The fleet is '''on''' the American coast.}}
##: {{ux|en|[[wikipedia:Croton-on-Hudson|Croton'''-on-'''Hudson]], [[wikipedia:Rostov-on-Don|Rostov'''-on-'''Don]], [[wikipedia:Southend-on-Sea|Southend'''-on-'''Sea]]}}
## Aboard (a mode of transport, especially public transport, or transport that one sits astride or uses while standing).
##: '''''on''' a bus'', '''''on''' a train'', '''''on''' a plane'', '''''on''' a ferry'', '''''on''' a yacht''
##: '''''on''' a bicycle'', '''''on''' a motorbike'',  '''''on''' a horse'', '''''on''' a scooter''
## {{label|en|nautical}} In the direction of (some part of one's vessel), to within 45 degrees.
##: {{ux|en|A ship was sighted '''on''' the {{m|en|port}} {{m|en|quarter}}.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''on''' the {{m|en|bow}}; '''on''' the {{m|en|starboard}} {{m|en|beam}}}}
# {{n-g|Expressing figurative placement, burden, or attachment.}}
#: {{ux|en|All of the responsibility is '''on''' him.}}
#: {{ux|en|I put a bet '''on''' the winning horse.}}
#: {{ux|en|You can't just spring a decision like that '''on''' me!}}
# {{n-g|Denoting physical contact or interaction with an object, such as impact or application of force.}}
## {{n-g|With verbs describing an action of pushing, pulling, pressing, etc., designates the thing to which force is applied.}}
##: ''tug '''on''' the rope''; ''push hard '''on''' the door''
## {{n-g|With verbs describing an action of hitting, rubbing, scratching, binding against, etc., designates the thing impacted or contacted.}}
##: {{ux|en|I stubbed my toe '''on''' an old tree stump.}}
##: {{ux|en|I caught my fingernail '''on''' the door handle.}}
##: {{ux|en|The rope snagged '''on''' a branch.}}
## {{n-g|Denoting performance or action by contact with the surface, upper part, or outside of anything}} By means of; with.
##: {{ux|en|to play '''on''' a violin or piano}}
# [[support|Supported]] by (the specified part of itself).
#: {{ux|en|A table can't stand '''on''' two legs.}}
#: {{ux|en|After resting '''on''' his elbows, he stood '''on''' his toes, then walked '''on''' his heels.}}
# {{lb|en|UK}} At (a certain value or level).
#: {{ux|en|The Tories are '''on''' twenty-five percent in this constituency.}}
#: {{ux|en|The blue team are '''on''' six points and the red team '''on''' five.}}
# At (a certain position within a sequence).
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''on''' question four.}}
# At or during the [[date]] or [[day]] of.
#: {{ux|en|Born '''on''' the 4th of July.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''On''' Sunday I'm busy. I'll see you '''on''' Monday.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can I see you '''on''' a different day?}}
# {{lb|en|UK|especially in sports reporting}} At (a given time after the start of something).
#: {{ux|en|Smith scored again '''on''' twelve minutes, doubling Mudchester Rovers' lead.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 24, 2011|author=Aled Williams|work=w:BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/14957961.stm|title=Chelsea 4-1 Swansea
|passage=The Spain striker had given Chelsea the lead '''on''' 29 minutes but was shown a straight red card 10 minutes later for a rash challenge on Mark Gower.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260103105412/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/14957961.stm}}
# At (an instant or cusp).
#: {{ux|en|'''on''' the stroke of midnight; '''on''' the "B" of "Bang!"}}
#: {{ux|en|'''on''' the point of leaving; '''on''' the verge of giving up}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Eyes of Max Carrados|passage=About two weeks ago I had another foretaste of success and immediately '''on''' it a veritable disaster.}}
# [[deal|Dealing]] with the [[subject]] of; [[about]]; [[concerning]].
#: {{ux|en|I was reading a book '''on''' history.}}
#: {{ux|en|The city hosted the World Summit '''on''' the Information Society}}
#: {{ux|en|I have no opinion '''on''' this subject.}}
#: {{ux|en|I onsidered the proposal '''on''' its merits.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''On''' the subject of staff changes, I have some news.}}
#* {{RQ:Trollope He Knew|volume=I|chapter=Lady Milborough as Ambassador|page=85|passage=[...] I received a note from that gentleman '''on''' a most trivial matter. I answered it as trivially.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating a means or medium.}}
#: {{ux|en|I saw it '''on''' television.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can't you see I'm '''on''' the phone?}}
#: {{ux|en|My favorite shows are '''on''' BBC America.}}
#: {{ux|en|The Beatles' appearance '''on''' the ''Ed Sullivan Show'' is '''on''' YouTube.}}
#: {{ux|en|The film was released '''on''' DVD.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll pay '''on''' card.}}
#: {{ux|en|He travelled '''on''' false documents.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating the target of, or thing affected by, an event or action.}}
#: {{ux|en|They planned an attack '''on''' London.}}
#: {{ux|en|The soldiers mutinied and turned their guns '''on''' their officers.}}
#: {{ux|en|Her words made a lasting impression '''on''' my mind.}}
#: {{ux|en|What will be the effect '''on''' morale?}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} In the possession of.
#: {{ux|en|I haven't got any money '''on''' me.}}
# Because of; [[on the basis of|upon the basis of]] (something not yet confirmed as true).
#: {{ux|en|to arrest someone '''on''' suspicion of bribery}}
#: {{ux|en|to contact someone '''on''' a hunch}}
# {{lb|en|also often '[[upon]]'}} At the time of (and often because of).
#: {{ux|en|'''On''' Jack's entry, William got up to leave.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''On''' the addition of ammonia, a chemical reaction begins.}}
# {{lb|en|also often '[[upon]]'}} Arrived or coming into the presence of.
#: {{ux|en|I need to get my planting done, as the season will soon be '''on''' us.}}
#: {{ux|en|Before we knew it, the forest was '''on''' us, and the air grew colder and damper.}}
# [[paid|Paid]] for by.
#: {{ux|en|The drinks are '''on''' me tonight, boys.}}
#: {{ux|en|The meal is '''on''' the house.}}
#: {{ux|en|I paid for the airfare and meals for my family, but the hotel room was '''on''' the company.}}
# [[toward|Toward]]; for; {{n-g|indicating the object of an emotion}}.
#: {{ux|en|Have pity or compassion '''on''' him.}}
# {{senseid|en|thirst on}} {{lb|en|especially|Ireland}} {{n-g|Indicating the person<!-- (etc.)--> experiencing an emotion, cold, thirst, hunger, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|I had a terrible thirst '''on''' me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2013-02-27|author=Rosemary Sutcliff|title=The Shining Company|publisher=Random House|isbn=9781448173679
|text='{{...}} the hunger is '''on''' me to carry my sword in distant places.' Mynyddog bowed his head.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2017-01-24|author=Ruth Gilligan|title=Nine Folds Make a Paper Swan|publisher=Tin House Books|isbn=9781941040508
|text=“Christ, the thirst '''on''' me.” “Sure, it's serious work, all that talk of independence.” The theater's stained-glass doors had first flung open in 1904, all in the hope of “rewriting the Irish identity,” of using culture in the fight{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2017-08-29|author=Ralph Peters|title=Judgment at Appomattox: A Novel|publisher=Forge Books|isbn=9780765381705|page=18
|text=“I've got the hunger '''on''' me, I do.” Riordan snorted. Hardly a man knew hunger as he did. The prison rations at Point Lookout, spare enough, had been a feast compared to the black years in Ireland.{{nb...}}}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating a means of subsistence or sustenance.}}
#: {{ux|en|They lived '''on''' ten dollars a week.}}
#: {{ux|en|The dog survived three weeks '''on''' rainwater.}}
#*: {{w|Go to work on an egg|Go to work '''on''' an egg.}}
# Engaged in or occupied with (an action or activity).
#: {{ux|en|He's '''on''' his lunch break.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''on''' nights all this week.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''on''' vacation; '''on''' holiday; '''on''' a mission; [[on the job|'''on''' the job]]; [[on the fiddle|'''on''' the fiddle]]}}
# {{senseid|en|a drug}} Regularly taking (a drug).
#: {{ux|en|You've been '''on''' these antidepressants far too long.}}
# {{senseid|en|influenced by a drug}} Under the influence of (a drug, or something that is causing drug-like effects).
#: {{ux|en|He's acting crazy because he's '''on''' crack right now.}}
# In addition to; besides; {{n-g|indicating multiplication or succession in a series}}.
#: {{ux|en|heaps '''on''' heaps of food}}
#: {{ux|en|mischief '''on''' mischief; loss '''on''' loss}}
# {{n-g|Indicating dependence or reliance}}.
#: {{ux|en|I depended '''on''' them for assistance.}}
#: {{ux|en|He will promise '''on''' certain conditions.}}
# Serving as a [[member]] of.
#: {{ux|en|He is '''on''' the jury; I am '''on''' the committee.}}
# By virtue of; with the pledge of.
#: {{ux|en|He affirmed or promised '''on''' his word, or '''on''' his honour.}}
## {{lb|en|informal|chiefly in [[set phrase]]s}} {{ellipsis of|en|[[I]] [[swear]] [[on]]}}: [[on my life]], [[on God]], on everything, [[etc.]]
# To the account or [[detriment]] of; {{n-g|denoting [[imprecation]] or invocation, or coming to, falling, or resting upon}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''On''' us be all the blame.}}
#: {{ux|en|A curse '''on''' him!}}
#: {{ux|en|Please don't tell '''on''' her and get her in trouble.}}
#: {{ux|en|He turned '''on''' her and has been her enemy ever since.}}
#: {{ux|en|He went all honest '''on''' me, making me listen to his confession.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|27|25||His blood be '''on''' vs, and '''on''' our children.}}
# {{lb|en|especially when numbers of combatants or competitors are specified}} [[against|Against]]; in [[opposition]] to.
#: {{ux|en|The fight was three '''on''' one, and he never stood a chance.}}
# {{lb|en|philosophy|logic}} [[according to|According to]], from the [[standpoint]] of; ({{n-g|expressing what must follow, whether accepted or not, if a given [[premise]] or [[system]] is assumed true}}).
#: {{syn|en|in|under|with|within}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021
|author=w:Gavin Ortlund
|title=Why God Makes Sense in a World That Doesn't: The Beauty of Christian Theism
|publisher=Baker Academic |location=Grand Rapids, MI |isbn=9781493432455
|passage='''On''' naturalism, it is therefore difficult to find a ground for ultimate moral hope.}}
# {{lb|en|snooker}} In a position of being able to pot (a given ball).
#: {{ux|en|All the way around the table, off four cushions, and ... and he's '''on''' the black!}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Having as identical [[domain]] and [[codomain]].
#: {{ux|en|a function '''on''' <math>\mathbb{R}</math>}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Having <math>V^n</math> as [[domain]] and ''V'' as [[codomain]], for the specified set ''V'' and some integer ''n''.
#: {{ux|en|an operator '''on''' <math>\mathbb{Z}</math>}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} [[generate|Generated]] by.
#: {{ux|en|the free group '''on''' four letters}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|Quebec}} [[divide|Divided]] by.
#: {{syn|en|over}}
#: {{ux|en|Twenty '''on''' three.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|dialect|regional}} [[of|Of]].
#: {{ux|en|I never seen 'im, and that's the truth '''on''' it.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|act=I|scene=ii|passage=Be not jealous '''on''' me.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|act=I|scene=iii|passage=Or have we eaten '''on''' the insane root / That takes the reason prisoner?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} At the peril of, or for the safety of.
#* {{RQ:Homer Dryden Iliad|title=Ilias 1|page=415|passage=Hence '''on''' thy life: the captive maid is mine; / Whom not for price or pray'rs I will reſign: [...]}}

